{
  "brand": "meituan",
  "recipe_version": "tofu.provider-offering-recipe/v1",
  "key": "meituan",
  "category": "relay",
  "name": "Meituan (AIGC Gateway)",
  "base_url": "https://aigc.sankuai.com/v1/openai/native",
  "faces": {
    "anthropic": {
      "base_url": "https://aigc.sankuai.com/v1/anthropic",
      "protocol": "anthropic"
    },
    "kunlun": {
      "base_url": "https://aigc.sankuai.com/v1",
      "protocol": "responses",
      "responses_profile": "compatible",
      "extra_headers": {
        "x-context-provider": "kunlun"
      },
      "inference_profile": {
        "sampling": {
          "temperature": "omit"
        },
        "features": {
          "responses_reasoning_replay": "supported"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "_kunlun_face_note": "THIRD face, added 2026-10-20 on live evidence. aigc.sankuai.com exposes an OpenAI-shaped Responses endpoint at /v1/responses beside the native chat face. Two facts measured on App **0733: (1) the public wire id gpt-6.1-sol is served but RPM-walled — repeated probes 0/20/40/60s apart all returned status=failed rate_limit_exceeded 'App:**0733在模型:gpt-6.1-sol每分钟请求次数超过限制'; (2) the Kunlun serving alias kunlunbedrock.gpt-6.1-sol-m17 returns 200 and streams, but ONLY with 'x-context-provider: kunlun' (without it: 200 + invalid_prompt '配置不存在'; on the chat face: 400 '配置不存在'; on gpt-6.1-sol with the same header: 400 '该模型在 provider 下无可用账号'). So the selector is per-DEPLOYMENT, not per-account: it lives on this face and reaches only the wire ids that pin face='kunlun' via the recipe's request_faces map. Do NOT lift these headers to the provider level — they 400 every other model on both other faces. The alias is not pinnable forever: '-m17' is a Kunlun revision, so it is a SEED entry in the pool rather than a replacement for the public id. This endpoint also REJECTS sampling: a request with temperature returns 400 \"Unsupported parameter: 'temperature' is not supported with this model\", so the face declares sampling.temperature='omit' (scoped to the face because that is where it was measured). Verified end to end through lib/llm/chat.py: model kunlunbedrock.gpt-6.1-sol-m17 + x-context-provider:kunlun + responses -> 'TOFU-OK' (22 tokens). REPLAY (added 2026-10-21): this face streams opaque 'reasoning' items carrying only encrypted_content — no summary text. A stateless Responses route that does NOT declare features.responses_reasoning_replay cannot re-send that item, so checked conversion refuses the whole next request as protocol_conversion:mandatory_continuity_unrepresentable and the Turn dies in request-prepare (observed in two live conversations at tool round 4-5). The endpoint both emits the item and serves the wire id that produces it, so replay is declared here rather than dropping the item: undeclared replay is exactly the closed-world default and is not a data problem.",
  "_extra_headers_note": "Do NOT re-add M-TransferContext-INF-CELL here. It pins every request to a named gray cell; when gray-release-ai-gpt-test was decommissioned on 2026-09-21 the whole provider 502'd (all models, both faces) while header-less clients stayed up. Gray cells are temporary by nature — the default must be the stable cell.",
  "_face_note": "ONE account, TWO wire faces. aigc.sankuai.com serves the same models over an OpenAI-compatible face (base_url, default) and an Anthropic-native face (faces.anthropic), sharing one set of API keys. Claude-family entries are routed to the anthropic face AUTOMATICALLY by lib/llm_dispatch/provider_face.resolve_face — they carry no per-model 'face' key, so a future opus-6/fable-6 is correct the day it is added. That face is the only one that emits thinking-block signature_delta (measured 2026-07-28: the OpenAI face streamed 111 chunks / 33 reasoning_content / 0 signature), and a thinking block replayed without its signature is rejected upstream. Do NOT delete faces.anthropic: a Claude entry with no anthropic face on this gateway is REFUSED at slot-build time rather than silently downgraded. kimi-k3 is ALSO pinned to the anthropic face (per-model 'face' key, 2026-09-10): its upstream is Anthropic-native, and the OpenAI face's translation layer started leaking Anthropic-protocol SSE frames (message_start/ping/content_block_*) into chat.completions streams at ~11:21 that day, poisoning Tofu's one-malformed-frame = untrustworthy-tool-stream guard. Probed live: POST /v1/anthropic/v1/messages model=kimi-k3 returns clean thinking+text, stream and non-stream.",
